<title>BELGIUM: SAPEC IN WINNING BID FOR PORTUGAL'S QUIMIGAL.</title>
<headline>SAPEC IN WINNING BID FOR PORTUGAL'S QUIMIGAL.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese firm Quimigest won the bidding for a 90 percent stake in state-owned chemicals group Quimigal-Quimica de Portugal SA with a 8.6 billion escudo offer.</p>
<p>The sale was approved at a cabinet meeting in Lisbon on Thursday.</p>
<p>Quimigest-Sociedade Quimica de Prestacao de Servicos is 75 percent owned by the Mello group. Belgian holding company Sapec SA was Mello's partner in the bidding.</p>
</text>
